<title>UK: Rank advances on hopes for share buy-back.</title>
<headline>Rank advances on hopes for share buy-back.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rank Group Plc shares built on early gains on Thursday, showing a 9p advance to 436-1/2p in brisk business by 1207 GMT, as hopes of a share buy-back grew, analysts said.</p>
<p>Reports highlighting the company's plans to sell its 20 percent stake in Rank Xerox, its joint venture with Xerox Corp for around 930 million stg, refreshed buy-back hopes, they said.</p>
<p>News that Rank plans to spend 1.5 billion stg over the next four to five years on UK leisure sites did not dampen speculation that cash from asset sales will be used to buy back stock in the market.</p>
<p>Analysts said Rank has been expected to reinvest heavily in its strong UK businesses for some time.</p>
<p>&quot;The most likely scenario is that they will do a big buy-back and although it's not new news these reports are putting it in front of the market again,&quot; said one analyst.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
